  {
    "episode_id": 95969,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95969.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 25,
    "turn_text": "A lot of the news since the weekend has been about President Biden seeming to open the door to this idea of tying worker crime to benefits, temporary aid to needy families, food stamps, Medicaid. I interpreted Biden's comments on Sunday in Rojobith as saying he was open to TANF. It's a smaller program. Medicaid was definitely a red line. And food stamps was kind of ambiguous. I don't think any of the comments from the White House have changed my analysis of that, just reading really closely everything they've said. One, I'm curious to see if you've read the tea leaves the same way and perhaps you have more information by talking to folks over there. And two, how concerning any of that is to you.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "A lot of recent news coverage has focused on President Biden appearing open to linking worker crime to public benefits like TANF, food stamps, and Medicaid.",
