      },
      {
        "text": "Medicaid is considered a non-negotiable boundary ('red line') by the speaker.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "The status of food stamps in relation to criminal penalties remains unclear or ambiguous according to the speaker.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "No subsequent White House statements have altered the speaker's interpretation of Biden's position.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "The speaker believes that policy shifts involving welfare programs should be evaluated based on their alignment with core principles like protecting vulnerable populations.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker trusts close textual analysis of official statements as sufficient evidence for interpreting political intentions.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker assumes that individuals within the White House may possess insider information not publicly available.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker views the potential linkage between criminal behavior and access to public assistance as a significant policy concern requiring careful evaluation.",
        "confidence": 0.86
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker expects the listener to share similar analytical frameworks for assessing political rhetoric and policy implications.",
        "confidence": 0.85
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Clarification Request (Specific)"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 95969,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95969.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 28,
    "turn_text": "Right. I do think it's pretty concerning. I think that the dynamics of the situation are such that if you are negotiating with an unknown entity, right? Kevin McCarthy does not know how many votes he has. He can't even go to the White House and say, if you give me this, I will have X votes. If you give me that, I'll have Y votes. And so when you start to open that door, when there is no concrete offer on the other side, it just kind of becomes a bank raid. They kind of go in and see what else is there on the table,",
